AU  - Zhang, XY
AU  - Zhang, PP
TI  - The Reciprocal Relationship Between Perceived Social Support and Compulsive Internet Use: A Daily Diary Study
T2  - BASIC AND APPLIED SOCIAL PSYCHOLOGY
AB  - BackgroundStudies confirm a negative relationship between compulsive Internet use and perceived social support, but the direction remains unclear.ObjectiveThis study explored the reciprocal relationship between the two among Chinese undergraduates.MethodOver 10 days, 167 participants (Mage = 19.75, 32.3% male) provided data on compulsive Internet use and perceived social support. On the first day, participants completed a baseline questionnaire, followed by nine consecutive days of daily diary surveys. A multilevel model estimated their relationship.ResultThe results of the cross-lagged analysis showed that perceived social support negatively predicted the onset of compulsive Internet use. When compulsive Internet use occurred, it further reduced perceived social support, showing a vicious circle.ConclusionThis study deepens the understanding of the reciprocal relationship and informs intervention strategies.
