AU  - Gámez-Guadix, M
AU  - Machimbarrena, JM
TI  - Internet risks and challenges among young adults and adolescents: an overview and research prospects / Riesgos y retos de Internet entre jóvenes y adolescentes: una visión general y perspectivas de investigación
T2  - JOURNAL FOR THE STUDY OF EDUCATION AND DEVELOPMENT
AB  - This article introduces the monographic issue of the Journal for the Study of Education and Development devoted to Internet challenges and risks among adolescents. It provides an overview of issues like the problematic use of the Internet and smartphones, cyberbullying, cyberhate and digital violence in different contexts, including intimate relationships. It also addresses sexual risks like sexting, grooming and sexual harassment facilitated by technology, as well as the spread of content on self-harm. It highlights the fact that these risks tend to be interrelated and share common vulnerability factors. The monograph includes studies with large samples and rigorous methodologies which analyse explanatory mechanisms like the search for social validation, body image and self-concept. This set of studies makes a significant contribution to our knowledge of digital risks while also underscoring the need to explore new challenges like those stemming from artificial intelligence and to develop culturally adapted preventive strategies.
   Este art & iacute;culo introduce el n & uacute;mero monogr & aacute;fico del Journal for the Study of Education and Development dedicado a los retos y riesgos de Internet entre adolescentes. Se ofrece una visi & oacute;n general de problem & aacute;ticas como el uso problem & aacute;tico de Internet y smartphones, el ciberacoso, el ciberodio y la violencia digital en distintos contextos, incluyendo relaciones de pareja. Tambi & eacute;n se abordan riesgos sexuales como el sexting, el grooming y el acoso sexual facilitado por tecnolog & iacute;a, as & iacute; como la difusi & oacute;n de contenido sobre autolesiones. Se destaca que estos riesgos suelen estar interrelacionados y compartir factores comunes de vulnerabilidad. El monogr & aacute;fico incluye estudios con muestras amplias y metodolog & iacute;as rigurosas, que analizan mecanismos explicativos como la b & uacute;squeda de validaci & oacute;n social, la imagen corporal y el autoconcepto. Este conjunto de investigaciones contribuye significativamente al conocimiento sobre riesgos digitales, subrayando tambi & eacute;n la necesidad de explorar nuevos desaf & iacute;os como los derivados de la inteligencia artificial y desarrollar estrategias preventivas culturalmente adaptadas.
